    {
      "id": "doezhl5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Major Universities in Punjab"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Panjab University was originally established in Lahore in 1882 before being relocated to Chandigarh post-partition.",
        "Punjab Agricultural University (PAU) at Ludhiana played a key role in ushering in the Green Revolution in India.",
        "Punjabi University in Patiala was founded in 1962 with the specific mandate to promote and develop the Punjabi language.",
        "Prominent national research institutions in Punjab include NIPER Mohali, IIT Ropar, and the Central University of Punjab in Bathinda."
      ],
      "id": "b44v1nq"
    },
